FRAME_CHI7|id=F2.2|n=2|E_G2=1:1|relation=EQUAL|E_H_predicted=1:1|reason=7 restricted to N is p_1 + ... + p_7 with the p_k distinct, and H permutes the 7 axes transitively, so the commutant of H on 7 is the scalars (Clifford); 7 is real, so the mean of chi_7^2 is the inner product of chi_7 with itself, which is 1|test=the mean over the 1344 elements of H of chi_7(h)^n|status=PREDICTION|claim=NAMED|json=0
FRAME_CHI7|id=F2.3|n=3|E_G2=1:1|relation=EQUAL|E_H_predicted=1:1|reason=the N-fixed tensors in 7 (x) 7 (x) 7 are spanned by e_i (x) e_j (x) e_k with p_i p_j p_k trivial, which holds exactly when i j k are distinct points of one Fano line: 7 lines times 6 orders gives 42 lines of tensors; H permutes them transitively, as GL(3,2) is 2-transitive on points and i j fix k, so they form a transitive monomial representation and the H-fixed space has dimension at most 1; the G2-fixed 3-form lies in it, so it is exactly the G2 value 1|test=the mean over the 1344 elements of H of chi_7(h)^n|status=PREDICTION|claim=NAMED|json=0
FRAME_CHI7|id=F2.4|n=4|E_G2=4:1|relation=GREATER_OR_EQUAL|E_H_lower_bound=5|E_H_exact=NOT_PREDICTED|reason=an extra invariant in Sym^4 of the 7 gives an extra invariant in 7 (x)4: Sym^4 of 7 has G2-fixed dimension 1:1 (G2_FIXED row, q^2 only); sum_i x_i^4 is H-fixed and not a multiple of q^2 (QUARTIC row), so the H-fixed symmetric tensors S have dimension at least 2; inside 7 (x)4 the G2-fixed space U meets S in the G2-fixed symmetric tensors, so the H-fixed space holds U + S, of dimension at least 4 + 2 - 1|test=the mean over H of chi_7(h)^4, predicted at least 5|status=PREDICTION|claim=NAMED|json=0
