FRAME_CHI14|id=F3.1|n=1|E_G2=0:1|relation=EQUAL|E_H_predicted=0:1|reason=14 sits in Wedge^2 of 7; e_i wedge e_j carries the N-character p_i p_j, which is p_k for the third point k of their line and so nontrivial; Wedge^2 of 7 has no N-fixed vector, hence 14 has no H-fixed vector|test=the mean over H of chi_14(h)^n|status=PREDICTION|claim=NAMED|json=0
FRAME_CHI14|id=F3.2|n=2|E_G2=1:1|relation=EQUAL|E_H_predicted=1:1|reason=Wedge^2 of 7 is 7 + 14 for G2 (NAMED; REFUTE.hbp lambda2_split_7_14 measured it) and restricts to N as 3 (p_1 + ... + p_7), so 14 restricts as 2 (p_1 + ... + p_7); the p_k part M_k of Wedge^2 is spanned by the 3 wedges over the 3 lines through k; the inertia group I_k (order 192, over the point stabiliser S_4) permutes those 3 lines 2-transitively through S_4 onto GL(2,2), so M_k is monomial with 2 double cosets and its self inner product is at most 2; M_k is (7)_k + (14)_k with (7)_k of dimension 1, which forces (14)_k irreducible for I_k; by Clifford 14 is induced from it and irreducible for H, and real, so the mean of chi_14^2 is 1|test=the mean over H of chi_14(h)^n|status=PREDICTION|claim=NAMED|json=0
